Schedule on the A75 cluster only (boot-arg sweetbigonly, default 1; sysctl kern.sweet_bigonly).
XNU sees one SMP cluster here (hw.nperflevels 1, the Clutch SMP scheduler); 0191's steering picks an A75 for user
threads only among idle CPUs, and all CPUs share one run queue, so CoreAnimation's render thread (backboardd
com.apple.coreanimation.display.primary, pri 54) kept landing on the in-order A55s at their 902 MHz cap. Measured
2026-10-29 on kernel 0255 with continuous home-page swipes (tools: sweetfg + swipe-trace.sh): all CPUs 29-31 fps,
median frame 25-29 ms; A75s only (kern.sched_update_recommended_cores=0xf0) 51-52 fps, median 16.4 ms, 78 % of frames
at 60 Hz, 3 % over 40 ms. Once all CPUs are up the cpufreq thread asks the scheduler, as CLPC's system request, to
recommend only the A75 cluster; kern.sweet_bigonly=0 recommends every CPU again, sweetbigonly=0 keeps them all.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
@@ -62,10 +62,16 @@
  *                                      sweetgpuinputms= in sweet_a630.c.
  *   sweetamp=0|1                       idle-core steering in the scheduler (default 1)
  *   sweetamp_prio=<n>                  base_pri threshold (default 31)
+ *   sweetbigonly=0|1                   A75 cluster only (0256, default 1; needs sweetamp): see below
  * Core-class steering (independent of the cpufreq mode): once all CPUs are up,
  * osfmk/kern/sched_prim.c is told which CPUs are A75 (MPIDR Aff1 >= 4) and which A55;
  * choose_processor() then gives user threads with base_pri >= sweetamp_prio an idle A75
  * first and all other threads (low QoS, kernel threads) an idle A55 first.
+ * A75 only (0256): the scheduler then recommends only the A75 cluster (CLPC's system request), so no thread that is
+ * not bound runs on an A55. The steering above picks among idle CPUs only, and all CPUs share one run queue, so
+ * CoreAnimation's render thread kept landing on A55s (in order, 902 MHz cap): continuous home swipes ran at 29-31 fps
+ * with all cores and at 51-52 fps (median frame 16.4 ms, 78 % of frames at 60 Hz) with the A75s only (2026-10-29).
+ * sysctl kern.sweet_bigonly (0/1) switches it at run time.
  * The closest LUT entry to the percentage is used (100 = highest index).
  * Starts once every selected CPU is up (after iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp's
  * SMP bring-up). All logs start with "SWEET CPUFREQ:".
